OBS207 SEATS - starting positions each shipped map will actually give,
  as the seat count rises. `_seats_changed` reverts a count the map
  refuses, so 'slots' below is what the match really generates.
  ladder.tres              42x48 authored_slots=4 :  2 seats->2 slots  4 seats->4 slots  6 seats->6 slots  8 seats->8 slots
  default.tres             168x194 authored_slots=20 :  2 seats->2 slots  4 seats->4 slots  6 seats->6 slots  8 seats->8 slots
  A seat past the slot count shares another seat's start. The two
  that share never found a base in any ladder match measured here.

  The REAL search, on real terrain, for the ladder map at 6 slots:
    seed 1: player_slots=6 -> 6 starting positions   validate_spawns: "" (silent)
    seed 2: player_slots=6 -> 6 starting positions   validate_spawns: "" (silent)
    seed 3: player_slots=6 -> 6 starting positions   validate_spawns: "" (silent)

