OBS207 LOOK - what a bot can say about criterion 5, which is
  otherwise the owner's. Player COLOUR is per player (D-052) and
  is not the civ's; what the civ decides is the MODEL, and four of
  six wear the primitive capsule for everything.
  civ          colour    authored models              primitive-tier archetypes
  emberdeep    #ad5c29   ["archers", "gatherers", "militia", "spearmen"] ["ram"]
  gildedreach  #c79e33   ["cavalry", "heavy_infantry"] ["archers", "engine", "gatherers", "general", "levy", "spearmen"]
  gravesworn   #b8bd9e   ["<none>"]                   ["engine", "gatherers", "general", "levy", "shades", "spearmen"]
  stoneblood   #738094   ["<none>"]                   ["breaker", "gatherers", "general", "heavy", "levy", "skirmishers"]
  thornwood    #386b47   ["<none>"]                   ["archers", "cavalry", "gatherers", "general", "greatbow", "levy"]
  windmarch    #b89961   ["<none>"]                   ["bowriders", "cavalry", "gatherers", "general", "levy", "skirmishers"]

  Civ colour is NOT what a player sees in a melee — D-052 gives the
  colour to the PLAYER, so two seats of the same civ are different
  colours and two seats of different civs may be adjacent hues. The
  civ's contribution to telling armies apart is its MODELS, and the
  table above is the whole of it.
